# The ONNX operators and types the daemon's models use, which are the only kernels
# compiled into OpenChime's minimal ONNX Runtime (scripts/build_onnxruntime.sh):
# Kitten mini v0.8 for read-aloud (ARCH-111) and Moonshine Tiny Streaming for
# voice input (ARCH-112). Generated by ONNX Runtime's create_reduced_build_config.py
# --format ORT --enable_type_reduction over every model file, with Kitten as
# converted on BOTH architectures (scripts/build_kitten.sh), because its
# conversions differ: on arm64 ONNX Runtime has half-precision kernels and keeps
# MatMul and Add in MLFloat16, where on amd64 it casts them to float. Moonshine's
# files are published already converted and are the same on both. Regenerate it
# when either model changes (docs/READ-ALOUD.md §4, docs/VOICE-INPUT.md §6). A
# kernel missing here makes a model fail to load, loudly, rather than run wrong.
